# Add Built-in Pixel Art Editor

This plan details the addition of a built-in 16x16 pixel art creation tool to the Minecraft Mod Maker, allowing users to create textures directly within the application.

## User Review Required

Please review the proposed UI design and integration of the pixel art creator. It will use a modal dialog with a 16x16 drawing grid and a JColorChooser for selecting colors. Once drawn, it will save the result to a temporary PNG file and use it as the selected texture, keeping the pre-existing "Browse" button functional.

## Proposed Changes

### UI & Core Logic

#### [NEW] [PixelArtDialog.java](file:///home/vladimir/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/minecraft_mod_maker/src/main/java/com/modmaker/PixelArtDialog.java)
- A new `JDialog` class that presents a modal window for pixel art generation.
- It will include a custom `JPanel` (the canvas) that renders a 16x16 grid. It will support mouse dragging to paint pixels.
- It will integrate a `JColorChooser` to let the user select drawing colors, and standard controls (Clear, Cancel, Save).
- The "Save" action will convert the 16x16 array of colors into a `BufferedImage`, write it to a temporary PNG file using `ImageIO`, and return this `File` to the caller.

#### [MODIFY] [ModMakerApp.java](file:///home/vladimir/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/minecraft_mod_maker/src/main/java/com/modmaker/ModMakerApp.java)
- In the `createBlockTab` method, add a "Create" button adjacent to the existing "Browse" button. Wiring it to display the `PixelArtDialog` and capture the created texture. 
- Do the same for the `createItemTab` method.
- Update `blockSelectedTexture` or `itemSelectedTexture` to the new temporary file on successful creation.

## Open Questions

- We're currently writing the drawn content to a temporary file (`File.createTempFile`). The temporary files are normally cleared when the OS decides, or on JVM exit if we mark them. Is this acceptable? Let me know if you would prefer them saved permanently in a specific directory!

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- No new automated tests are planned. The pixel art rendering and file persistence logic will be verified manually.

### Manual Verification
- We will start the `ModMakerApp` UI.
- Verify block tab: clicking "Create" opens the pixel UI, drawing a small design, saving it assigns the path correctly.
- Ensure importing a pre-made image with "Browse" still works correctly in both tabs.
